  "script": "I'm an amateur codebreaker, and this is the one we all grew up on. In 1969 the Zodiac killer mailed a three hundred and forty character cipher to the San Francisco Chronicle. For fifty-one years, nobody could read it. Then in December 2020, three amateurs cracked it. A software developer in Virginia, a mathematician in Australia, and a warehouse worker in Belgium. The message taunted the police. The killer has still never been identified. But amateurs did that. Remember it, next time someone tells you that you can't figure things out."
